966	 * archive opened with fromWritableBuffer is modified and closed (double_free_report.pdf).
967	 *
968	 * close() must read the rewritten archive back into a freshly allocated buffer instead
969	 * of reusing/realloc'ing the very buffer that backs the libzip source. The crafted input
970	 * below makes the rewrite exceed the original buffer length, which forces the buffer to
971	 * grow inside close() - the exact path that used to free the source-backed buffer twice.
